zink: depth clamp with core depthClamp, without depth_clip_enable

zink now offers depth_clip_disable (GL_ARB_depth_clamp) also when the
device has core depthClamp but not VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable, and warns
about the missing extension only for a clip/clamp combination core
Vulkan cannot express (clip == clamp). GL only asks for clip == !clamp,
and without the extension Vulkan disables depth clipping exactly when
depthClampEnable is set, which zink already derives from the rasterizer
state. MoltenVK 1.4.2 has depthClamp but not the extension, so zink
exposed no depth clamp at all: OpenMW's shadow pass enables
GL_DEPTH_CLAMP unconditionally (GL_INVALID_ENUM on every draw) and
shadow casters outside the light frustum's depth range were clipped.
Devices with the extension are unchanged.

Upstream: not submitted; same condition in Mesa 26.2.3.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -921,7 +921,10 @@
 
    caps->max_texture_array_layers = screen->info.props.limits.maxImageArrayLayers;
 
-   caps->depth_clip_disable = screen->info.have_EXT_depth_clip_enable;
+   /* without VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable, core depthClampEnable also disables depth clipping: that is the only
+    * combination GL asks for (clip == !clamp, no separate near/far), see zink_create_gfx_pipeline
+    */
+   caps->depth_clip_disable = screen->info.have_EXT_depth_clip_enable || screen->info.feats.features.depthClamp;
 
    caps->shader_stencil_export = screen->info.have_EXT_shader_stencil_export;
 
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_pipeline.c
@@ -175,7 +175,8 @@
    if (screen->info.have_EXT_depth_clip_enable) {
       depth_clip_state.pNext = rast_state.pNext;
       rast_state.pNext = &depth_clip_state;
-   } else {
+   } else if (hw_rast_state->depth_clip == hw_rast_state->depth_clamp) {
+      /* core Vulkan clips exactly when it does not clamp */
       static bool warned = false;
       warn_missing_feature(warned, "VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable");
    }
